{
  "baseline_version": "v1.2.0",
  "frozen_at_utc": "2026-05-25T16:05:42.317764+00:00",
  "summary": "First reproducible baseline of the TCGA-GBM nerve-cell pipeline.\nPipeline: GDC loom \u2192 QC \u2192 scVI integration \u2192 CNV-based malignancy labelling \u2192\nnerve-cell subset (re-clustered on X_scVI, 24 Leiden clusters) \u2192\nDE markers (Wilcoxon) \u2192 offline GSEA (gseapy.prerank vs MSigDB C5 GO BP+MF, v2024.1.Hs) \u2192\ncluster annotations / clinical association / tumor\u2013nerve LIANA interactions /\ninteractive marimo enrichment explorer.\nBatch-correction QC: 18 / 24 clusters PASS (median dominant-sample fraction 0.313;\nmedian normalised entropy 0.722 of 4.087 bits).\n\nv1.1.0 deltas (2026-05-24, post failing-cluster diagnosis):\n- cl21 dropped from downstream _with_qc.csv tables via\n  nerve_cells.batch_qc.exclude_clusters (dissociation artifact:\n  stress-marker dominant \u2014 MT-RNR2/1, RPL41, B2M, FTH1; see\n  markdowns/failing_cluster_diagnosis.md).\n- Ependymal added as 5th cell-type label (FOXJ1/RFX3/DNAH7-9-11/\n  CFAP54/PIFO/RSPH1 marker set) and to nerve_cells.cell_types so\n  cells pass the nerve_cell_subset filter. After re-clustering with\n  the +5,713 ependymal cells, three ependymal-dominant clusters\n  emerged: cl11 (72% ependymal, 2,585 cells), cl15 (89%, 1,854 cells),\n  and cl19 (83%, 1,020 cells; clean motile-cilia signature CFAP54/\n  DNAH7/DNAH9). cl11 and cl15 were not predicted by the cut doc;\n  they represent biologically distinct ependymal subpopulations.\n- scANVI v2 retrained on 5 labels (was 4 + Unknown): astrocyte 22,600\n  / neuron 20,538 / ependymal 14,545 / oligodendrocyte 14,380 /\n  opc 13,219 + Unknown 21,321. Classifier accuracy 0.85 (was 0.84).\n- notebooks/02_nerve_enrichment_explorer.py: added 'ependymal' theme\n  regex (CILIUM/CILIARY/AXONEMAL/DYNEIN/EPENDYM) to surface cl11/15/19\n  ciliary GSEA hits in the theme roll-up.\n- v1.0.0 baseline (provenance/baseline_v1.0.0.json) remains frozen\n  and citable.\n\nv1.2.0 deltas (2026-05-24, ependymal panel tightening + freeze insulator):\n- Ependymal panel tightened to DNAH7/DNAH9/DNAH11/CFAP54/PIFO/RSPH1.\n  FOXJ1 dropped (absent from var_names, unscoreable); RFX3 dropped\n  (non-discriminating, 61-97% across astrocyte clusters). PIFO retained\n  for intent but also absent from var_names -> 5 effective scoring genes.\n- Freeze insulator added (nerve_cells.frozen_subset_file ->\n  provenance/nerve_subset_v1_1_0.txt; SHA256 26ea29171a6807efa6a7ed05c18\n  cbc60578f3434f76033bb56a06677d8581a79; 106,603 barcodes) so the panel\n  change cannot cascade into cell_type_predicted -> nerve_cell_subset ->\n  nerve_leiden cluster IDs. Rerun was bit-exact: 0 cells drifted,\n  per-cluster sizes identical to v1.1.0 (54/54 Snakemake steps, ~5h 14m\n  on M4 Max / MPS).\n- Refactor: is_nerve_marker annotation + gene_presence.csv moved from\n  loom_to_h5ad to scrna_qc, so future panel changes no longer trigger\n  per-sample reruns.\n- scANVI v2 retrained on tightened-panel labels: astrocyte 22,927 /\n  Unknown 21,321 / neuron 20,420 / oligodendrocyte 14,358 /\n  ependymal 14,280 / opc 13,297. Classifier accuracy 0.8446.\n- Panel-tightening predictions in the v1.1.0 failing_cluster_diagnosis\n  supplement were partially wrong: cl15 ependymal-predicted stayed at\n  90.1% (not 30-60% as forecast) and score_ependymal mean rose\n  (0.193 -> 0.265). Root cause: sc.tl.score_genes is non-monotonic in\n  panel size + cluster-level argmax is robust to per-cell shifts.\n  cl15 MIXED-cluster finding documented; surgical sub-cluster relabel\n  deferred to v1.3.0. See markdowns/DO_THIS_NEXT_post_v1.2.0_rerun.md\n  and the supplement's \"Post-rerun reality check\" subsection.\n- v1.0.0 and v1.1.0 baselines remain frozen and citable.\n",
